{
  // The extension type check — M025 T001.
  //
  // `npm run check` used to cover the root scripts, the skill trees, the panel and the
  // companion package, and nothing checked `extension/` — the content scripts, the overlay,
  // the relay and the picker agent, the code that runs inside a user's inspected page. This
  // config is what closes that gap; `check:extension` runs it from `npm run check`.
  //
  // Two settings are deliberate and must not be read as sloppiness:
  //
  // - `exclude: ["panel/**"]` is the only exclusion, and it is not a source tree. `extension/
  //   panel/` holds build output — `main.js`, `worker-*.js` and the `chunk-*.js` files — written
  //   by the panel build (`npx nx run angular-ai-devtools:build-extension`). It contributes 187
  //   of the 220 non-strict errors in the directory, and every one of them measures the
  //   bundler's output, not the source anyone edits. A check over it would be red forever for
  //   a tree that cannot be fixed at source. No authored file is excluded: `include` is the
  //   whole `extension/` tree, as N2 requires.
  // - `strict: false` is deliberate, not an oversight. `strict: true` over the same sources
  //   reports 7308 errors, almost all implicit-any in hand-written JavaScript that has never
  //   been annotated; making the extension strict-clean is a rewrite, not a milestone step. The
  //   gap is recorded here rather than hidden, and the check still catches the real defects a
  //   wrong property access produces (N4: the extension is not claimed strict-clean).
  //
  // `@types/chrome` supplies the extension API globals (`chrome.runtime`, `chrome.devtools`, …)
  // so `TS2304 Cannot find name 'chrome'` is not among the reported errors. It is a
  // devDependency: it types the check and never enters the built extension.
  //
  // `types: ["chrome"]` keeps the ambient set to exactly that: without it every `@types`
  // package installed for the workspace (node, ws, …) would leak into content-script scope and
  // report errors the browser would never raise.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": false,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "preserve",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["chrome"],
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  },
  "include": ["**/*.js"],
  "exclude": ["panel/**"]
}
